infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Write model vs read model: why one can't serve both
  desc Normalization serves writes; denormalization serves reads — forced into one model, each degrades the other
  compares
    - label Write model (command side)
      children
        - label Normalized
          desc Invariants checked over a minimal, consistent dataset
        - label Invariant-guarding
          desc Rejects a command that would break a business rule
        - label Aggregate-shaped, transactional
          desc One consistency boundary the write must pass through
        - label Handles commands
          desc Intent in, domain event out — returns no view data
    - label Read model (query side)
      children
        - label Denormalized
          desc Pre-joined row — no aggregate graph to load and discard
        - label View-shaped
          desc Returns the exact DTO one screen needs in a single fetch
        - label No invariants
          desc Fields only have to be correct and fast
        - label Answers queries
          desc No side effects — safe to call any number of times
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
